35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, the bank statements were a bit of a wake-up call! A lot of people struggled to pay all at once. Also, most of our costs are fixed, so we need a steady income regardless of turnout.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"That is concerning, @Mio. I've found that introducing door charges actually drove people away from weekday meetings. It seems that when members stop feeling a sense of ownership, they simply stop coming.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"I knew it. A tiny group of us are doing all the work and attending everything, while eighteen people didn't show up once. It's completely unfair that everyone pays the same when so few actually contribute.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The administrative burden is significant. Chasing individual session payments takes six times longer than yearly collections, and mid-year joiners require tedious manual calculations. We must avoid a system that creates an unsustainable workload for the treasurer.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I've found some really important things! People who didn't join said they hate paying for a whole year upfront. Also, those ""named grades"" from the past caused a lot of friction and made some people feel less welcome.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, if chasing individual payments is that much work, we definitely can't do a pay-as-you-go system. But @Kenji, if people hate paying upfront, we're in a real bind! How do we balance that?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we are caught between a need for simplicity and a need for accessibility. If door charges discourage attendance, yet upfront costs deter new members, we must find a middle ground that preserves the club's welcoming spirit.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, a ""middle ground"" sounds like it just keeps things unfair. If eighteen people aren't even showing up, why are we worrying about making it easier for them? We should reward the people actually doing the work.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, rewarding the active members is a goal, but not at the cost of the treasurer's sanity. Any system that requires constant tracking of individual attendance for billing will be rejected by whoever takes the role.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I get that it feels unfair, but if we make it too strict, we might lose the people who just need a bit more time to settle in. We want the club to grow, right?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I agree with @Kenji! We can't just ignore the newcomers. But @Toshio is right; we can't kill the treasurer with paperwork. Since 70% of our costs are fixed, we need a reliable base of money. How do we do that without scaring people off?","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Perhaps we should consider how the structure affects the psychology of belonging. If a high upfront fee is a barrier, but per-event charges make members feel like guests rather than owners, we need a solution that feels inclusive yet stable.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm tired of talking about ""feelings"" while nine people do all the setup and locking up. If we don't address the fact that a few are carrying the whole club, those nine people will eventually quit too.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, your point about the core group is valid, but we cannot solve it by creating a bookkeeping nightmare. A system that requires tracking every single visit for billing is a recipe for failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I don't want the hard workers to quit! But if we make people feel like they're being graded or judged on how often they come, it might just make the club feel cold. We need something friendly!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"It sounds like we're all worried about different things, but we agree that the current way isn't working. We need a stable base for those fixed costs, but something that doesn't feel like a wall to new people.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It is clear that we must avoid any system that makes members feel like temporary visitors. If we prioritize the feeling of belonging, we may find a way to balance the financial needs with the human ones.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not interested in ""belonging"" if it means the same nine people are being taken advantage of. If we don't find a way to make the cost reflect the actual usage, we're just ignoring the problem.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"We must be pragmatic. We have a conflict between the treasurer's capacity, the members' willingness to pay upfront, and the desire for fairness. Any option that increases manual tracking is a non-starter for me.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I just hope we can find a way to be fair to the hard workers without making the club feel like a business. Let's look at the options and pick the friendliest one!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
