60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Looking at the options, C seems like a nightmare for the treasurer and might drive people away, as @Jonathan found. A is stable for our fixed costs, but @Kenji, would it be too scary for newcomers?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I believe Option C is far too risky. My findings show that door charges erode the sense of ownership and discourage attendance. We must avoid making our members feel like guests in their own club.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option A is just more of the same unfairness. Option B lets us acknowledge different levels of use. If we have tiers, the people doing all the work aren't just subsidizing ghosts.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is problematic. @Kenji mentioned that named grades caused friction in the past. Furthermore, managing different tiers and their scopes of activities could increase the administrative burden I am so concerned about. Option A is the most efficient.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,@Toshio is right about the friction! I'm really worried Option B would make people feel judged. But Option A is what scared away the taster guests. Is there any way to make A more flexible?,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, we can't change the options, but maybe we can agree to be flexible with how we collect the flat fee? @Toshio, if we stick with A, it's the easiest for the treasurer, right?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If we prioritize the psychological well-being of our members, Option A is the safest. It removes the transactional feeling of Option C and avoids the social stratification of Option B, fostering a true sense of community.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, ""community"" doesn't mean ignoring the fact that some people are being used. Option A is just a way to keep the ghosts happy while the nine of us do everything. I'm voting for B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, your desire for fairness is noted, but Option B creates social divisions and administrative complexity. Option A is the only choice that ensures the treasurer's role remains sustainable and the club's fixed costs are covered.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I don't want anyone to feel judged or divided, so I can't support B. C is too much work and feels cold. A is the friendliest, even if it's a bit scary at first!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm leaning towards A too. It's the only way to guarantee we cover those fixed costs without guessing. @Takumi, I know it feels unfair, but is a little unfairness worse than the club collapsing?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe it is. If we prioritize a rigid sense of fairness over the spirit of the club, we risk losing the very peace and belonging that make this place special. Option A is the most gentle path.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"It's not ""rigid fairness,"" it's basic respect for the people actually keeping this place alive. If we just ignore the ghosts, we're telling the hard workers their time doesn't matter. I'm sticking with B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the ""respect"" you seek cannot be built on a system that burns out the treasurer. Option A is the only pragmatic choice that balances financial stability with administrative viability. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with @Toshio and @Jonathan! I don't want anyone to feel like they're in a ""lower grade."" Let's go with Option A and just be really nice about how we ask for the money!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I agree! Option A is the most stable for our budget and the easiest for the treasurer. I'm sorry it doesn't solve everything, @Takumi, but it's the safest bet for the club's future. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I concur. While it may not satisfy every desire for equity, it preserves the harmony and accessibility of our community. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,You're all just choosing the easy way out. I'll vote for B because it's the only one that actually addresses the imbalance. But don't be surprised when the people doing all the work get fed up. I vote B.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,The decision is clear. We must prioritize the sustainability of the club's management and its financial stability over a flawed sense of equity. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for Option A too! It's the best way to keep everyone feeling equal and welcome, and we can just help people out if they struggle with the payment. Option A it is!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
